#
# A .properties value continues onto the next line after an odd number of trailing backslashes, so a
# changed line belongs to the key its logical line starts with. In gradle.properties only the continued
# value changes. In app/gradle.properties a backslash added to the line before folds the jacoco key into
# another key's value, so the floor is gone. In config/coverage.properties the hunk starts on a changed
# line that may continue a key above it the diff doesn't show; the guard can't tell, so it fails closed.

